=== A1 (P-23a) the variance relation is the generic small-noise expansion, for ANY drift f ===
  Delta c2 for arbitrary drift f: T*Derivative(f(a), (a, 2))  -> O(noise) mean shift = (1/2) int g f''(mu) v ds
  quartic C-B drift: T f''(a) = -24*T*a*beta (record: -24 beta T a)
  double-well x - x^3 (non-GRUT): T f''(a) = -6*T*a  -> same relation form, (S-D) = -3 int g mu v

=== B1 (P-23) the one law-level lock on record: interior family mu=1+x*al, eta=1/(1+x*al), Sigma=(mu(1+eta))/2 ===
  Sigma = alpha*x/2 + 1 ;  Sigma0 - mu0/2 = 0  (x and alpha both eliminated)
  mu*eta = 1  (curvature potential Phi unmodified; only Psi modified)
  f(R) small-scale: mu=4/3, eta=1/2 -> Sigma = 1 (Sigma0 = 0; off the GRUT line Sigma0 = mu0/2)

=== B2 (P-23) CM of the retained response: symmetric K (reversible) vs cycle affinity (record E-4) ===
  symmetric K_b-type block: eigenvalues real: True -> k(t) = sum u^2 e^{-lam t} is CM (Debye/reversible: standard)
  3-ring with affinity: eigenvalues [0.+0.j     3.+1.3856j 3.-1.3856j] -> complex pair, k(t) oscillates, not CM (standard: broken detailed balance)

=== B3 (P-23 charter) decoherence-rate mass exponent moves with supplied geometry / correlation length ===
  correlation length l= 50.0: d ln Gamma / d ln m over m=8->64->512 : 2.000, 1.999
  correlation length l=  2.0: d ln Gamma / d ln m over m=8->64->512 : 1.840, 1.558
  correlation length l=  0.3: d ln Gamma / d ln m over m=8->64->512 : 1.042, 1.020
  -> exponent 2 (coherent, R << l) ... 1 (incoherent, R >> l): set by supplied R/l, shared by DP/CSL/any mass-density coupling
